Analyze this {language} code for unsafe deserialization and data integrity failures (OWASP A08).

Source file:
{source}

Already reported by mechanical pattern analysis — do NOT report these again:
{known_findings}

Detect:
- Untrusted input deserialized into arbitrary object graphs
- Type information taken from the payload instead of being fixed by the code
- XML parsed with DTD or external entity resolution enabled (XXE)
- Archive extraction without path validation (zip slip)
- Signature or checksum not verified before using downloaded content
- Deserialization callbacks or constructors with side effects
- Recursive or unbounded payloads accepted without a size or depth limit

Return a JSON array of findings. Each finding:
{{
  "issue_type": "UNSAFE_DESERIALIZATION|POLYMORPHIC_TYPE|XXE|ZIP_SLIP|UNVERIFIED_CONTENT|SIDE_EFFECT_CALLBACK|UNBOUNDED_PAYLOAD|OTHER",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "description": "one sentence describing the specific issue",
  "fix": "concrete fix suggestion"
}}

Return [] if no issues found. Return ONLY the JSON array, no prose.
